# Design: Email Two-Factor Authentication (v1) + Verification-Code Hardening

- Status: Approved for implementation
- Date: 2026-10-19
- Target repo: `cybernetics-data-centre` (Teable-based app; NestJS backend + Next.js pages-router frontend)
- Delivered as: one PR

## 1. Decisions

| # | Question | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Should social logins (Google / GitHub / OIDC) be challenged? | **No, not in v1.** 2FA applies to email + password sign-in only. The UI copy says so. |
| 2 | Scope | **Full stack**: settings UI, API, data model, sign-in challenge, emails, i18n, tests. |
| 3 | Verification codes leaking through JWTs (signup, change-email) | **Fix in the same PR** with one shared verification-code service, which 2FA also uses. |

## 2. Background

### 2.1 Where the feature lives

