Props: `{ action: 'enable' | 'disable'; children: ReactNode }` (the trigger). Two steps inside one `Dialog`, `md:w-[400px]`, the same as `ChangeEmailDialog`:

```
Step 1: Confirm it's you            Step 2: Enter the code
┌─────────────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ Turn on two-factor auth     │     │ Check your email            │
│ We'll email a 6-digit code  │     │ We sent a code to           │
│ to a•••••e@gmail.com.       │     │ a•••••e@gmail.com           │
│                             │     │                             │
│ Current password            │     │   [_][_][_]-[_][_][_]       │
│ [••••••••••]                │     │                             │
│                             │     │ Didn't get it? Resend (27s) │
│ [Send code]                 │     │ [Confirm]       [Back]      │
└─────────────────────────────┘     └─────────────────────────────┘
```

Behaviour:

- `useMutation(sendTwoFactorEmailCode)`. On success: store `token`, go to step 2, start `useCutDown` with `twoFactorSendCodeMailRate`.
- `InputOTP` (6 slots, `inputMode="numeric"`, `autoComplete="one-time-code"`). Submits automatically when all 6 are filled, and Confirm is also available.
- `useMutation(enableTwoFactorEmail | disableTwoFactorEmail)`. On success: `toast.success`, `useSession().refresh()`, close and reset the dialog. No reload or sign-out.
- Errors map to inline `<Error>` with `meta: { preventGlobalError: true }`: `INVALID_CREDENTIALS` → "Password is incorrect"; `INVALID_CAPTCHA` → "Code is invalid or expired"; `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` → existing rate-limit message with `{seconds}`; `CONFLICT` → refresh the session and close (state changed in another tab).
- Resend calls send-code again with the password kept in state. Closing the dialog clears all state, including the password.
- Disable copy: title "Turn off two-factor authentication", with a warning line "Your account will only be protected by your password."

### 8.3 Login (`features/auth/components/SignForm.tsx`)

- `onError`: add `case HttpErrorCode.TWO_FACTOR_REQUIRED:` → `setTwoFactorChallenge(error.data)`.
- When `twoFactorChallenge` is set, the form shows a code step instead of email and password:

```
Check your email
We sent a 6-digit sign-in code to a•••••e@gmail.com

      [_][_][_]-[_][_][_]

[Verify]
Resend code (30s)   ·   Use a different account
```

- Verify → `signinTwoFactor({ challengeId, code })`. On success, run the same path as a normal sign-in (`onSuccess?.()` + existing redirect handling).
- Resend → `resendSigninTwoFactor({ challengeId })`, which replaces the challenge and restarts the countdown.
- `INVALID_CAPTCHA` → "That code isn't right." Expired → reset to the password step with "Your code expired, sign in again." `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (lockout) → existing lockout message.
- "Use a different account" clears the challenge and returns to the password form, keeping the email filled in.
- Sub-component: `features/auth/components/TwoFactorCodeStep.tsx`, so `SignForm` doesn't grow by 100+ lines.

