## 9. Security summary

| Threat | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Stolen password | Sign-in also needs a code from the account's inbox. |
| Stolen session cookie used to turn off 2FA | Disabling needs the password **and** an emailed code. |
| Brute-forcing a code | 6 digits, 5 guesses per token, 10-minute expiry, send rate limit per email, wrong 2FA codes count toward the existing account lockout. |
| Reading a code from the token | Tokens are opaque random values. Codes are stored as an HMAC on the server (section 4). This also fixes signup and change-email. |
| Replaying a code | Single use: the entry is deleted on success. |
| Timing attack on compare | `timingSafeEqual`. |
| Lock-out on a server without SMTP | Enabling is blocked when `mailConfigured` is false. Disabling is always allowed. |
| User enumeration through the 2FA step | The challenge only appears **after** a correct password, so it reveals nothing new. |
| Silent change by an attacker | Notice email on every enable or disable. |

**Out of scope, flagged:** `auth.config.ts` falls back to a hard-coded `jwt.secret` (and session secret / access-token key) when env vars are missing. The HMAC uses `jwt.secret`, so production **must** set `BACKEND_JWT_SECRET` / `SECRET_KEY`. Worth a separate ticket to refuse to start in production on default secrets.

## 10. Edge cases

| Case | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Change email while 2FA is on | Allowed. The new address is proven by its own code (now leak-free), and 2FA codes go to the new address afterwards. |
| Password reset while 2FA is on | Reset clears all sessions, as today. The next sign-in still needs a 2FA code, which goes to the same inbox. |
| Social login for a user with 2FA on | Not challenged (decision 1). The UI copy says so. |
| User deactivated, or 2FA turned off mid-challenge | `POST /signin/two-factor` reloads the user and rejects a deactivated account. If 2FA was turned off in between, the code is still accepted, which is harmless. |
| Several tabs | The settings `CONFLICT` refreshes the session. Login challenges are independent tokens. |
| User adds a password later (social-only account) | The row becomes active after `AddPassword` signs them out and back in. |
| Deleting the account | Columns go with the row. Cache entries expire on their own. |

